  "source_identity": {
    "canonical_url": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/pregnancy/halfway-pregnancy",
    "source_record_id": "raw_html_7e7d131e9bf4bc9d",
    "udare_article_path": "C:\\Users\\HP\\Documents\\LinkCraftor\\backend\\server\\data\\udare_store\\ws_whattoexpect_com\\articles\\pregnancy-halfway-pregnancy_7e7d131e.html",
    "udare_article_sha256": "fa52751ecba538971442cee9f569100d4792d9dddf01648a45c1291faf00724f"
  },
  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/pregnancy/halfway-pregnancy",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 26,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "These moms came up with some creative ways to celebrate the 20-week mark.",
        "text_sha256": "906faca3fd7b2d48ac256e64d33507c4d8c791d3b46fc8bf1aa15762c7075fc0",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "By the time you're 20 weeks pregnant, you've made it through those wild weeks full of nausea , weird cravings , and \"is this normal\" Google searches. To honor this midpoint, maybe you'll queue up Bon Jovi's \"Livin' on a Prayer\" and scream, \"Whoaaa, we're halfway there!\" at the top of your lungs, or maybe run out to the market for a pint of Ben and Jerry's appropriately named flavor, Half Baked.",
        "text_sha256": "f422291539018b25eb579a49e31a5e51ef32ced1ce5a5f488cae17c47a59c1fb",
        "word_count": 72
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Each and every pregnancy milestone is worth celebrating, which is why these trending 20-week photoshoot ideas are oh-so-sweet. Whether you want to keep it simple with a quick selfie or mark the milestone with a sweet treat, find inspiration in these sweet, punny, and downright adorable ways moms are commemorating this special time.",
        "text_sha256": "1f0c0f0f9f03d80c1e4fece73b8c9fcd8b70b3751090d28b6a7df7a5151221af",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Bake some cookies",
        "text_sha256": "cf8c262e30e7295dcf66d0710b73ace356e182998d2f46de3b42cc2e11fda105",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "overhead view of a pregnant mom posing next to some flour on a kitchen countertop with the words",
        "text_sha256": "0986465b3b39abed9cb77a8a432bbfee6339844506b5ad9e76cb97b7ba54651e",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Mom-to-be Kayla Djukic ( @kayladjukic ) grabbed some cookies, a few sonograms, and a bag of flour for her take on the \"half-baked\" trend. \"You don't have to put a lot of effort or money into it,\" Djukic says. \"I was lucky that I have a friend who is a photographer ( @sarahbiez) , but you can ask your partner to take the photos on your phone, or even set up a tripod!\"",
        "text_sha256": "96cf05cfe1ba427cb801b9bdeb3773435022ccc522fa66b83a5ed7a00fa96cc0",
        "word_count": 73
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Find out what size fruit your baby is",
        "text_sha256": "00f4156dc3f9713643b5a656b7d0aaf3c8413bf9d70edb9a5ae441fb29c55127",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "pregnant mom posing with a banana next to her belly to represent the size of her baby",
        "text_sha256": "77c1298e751dfe0523978524719e7604f3cebc27f94af3588d3a992114edb1c8",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Every week, you can open the What to Expect app and find out how big your baby is now, not just in inches, but also in fruit. ( Week 8 is raspberry … Week 34 is pineapple.) Krisie Schoppaul ( @mrs.schoppaul ) took this feature to heart by marking the midway point with a banana.",
        "text_sha256": "f133283359770b7e225bc2dabf96131a5d2e1bd7d9e4d55cab7428949f0f9ce1",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Try something savory",
        "text_sha256": "cac33bbde32ebe029bec8091d6f4a7e67a348c160f860bd8255c0484633363c8",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "pregnant mom posing with a can of baked beans",
        "text_sha256": "1fb06c113f454932f44803abb371fca084f221c9e5293d6491cc998808a0174c",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In a What to Expect Community forum, mom-to-be Tanya McLaughlin shared her unique \"half-baked\" idea for a 20-week photoshoot: posing with a can of baked beans. \"We still call him Bean,\" she says. \"It's a hard habit to break.\"",
        "text_sha256": "01b5d8bc995d845859752e5fb1ac5e26b90f7f976537f1cc0f9c7a0fb920bbcc",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Make a bouquet",
        "text_sha256": "d9438c324f05776bb307be3025547e1e2c21b6674cea7056fc336d3c4f410631",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "side view of a pregnant mom holding a bouquet of pink flowers up to her face",
        "text_sha256": "3f88df15f9a44d8988adace85480ae2a83215ac047978e5b513f8ec7d516a5b9",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Perhaps the freshest take on the half-baked trend comes from mom-to-be Kylie Russell ( @kybooktok ), whose friend Amy Holladay snapped some photos of her belly with flowers. \"I've always been into capturing memories with photos,\" she says. \"I also thought 'half-bloomed' was especially cute with us having a spring due date.\"",
        "text_sha256": "11c868c3b12391af5afe38c516ed36ae18b561e6c26acd3f3e452c48c3b9f3f4",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Russell says she added her own blooms to a premade bouquet and also used it as a gender reveal . (She chose mostly pink flowers because they’re expecting a girl.)",
        "text_sha256": "dd559a7eb4af9d9ae87faeb89f3fd645eeed9f9b8a49b62e21d071ccb319cf91",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Get your older kid in on the action",
        "text_sha256": "cf7bd86c3dece0a25f499e0e3cfd8dcab590ac589e894dba26359ea0ebd492c9",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "pregnant mom and her toddler son posing with a series of ultrasound photos and a pint of Ben and Jerry's Half Baked ice cream",
        "text_sha256": "e335f0bd4d0eddc0ac5d6e74d03b81aa665edb5d0285e4a17856754dd0612504",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There were two main requirements for Bijou Nguyen: a pint of Ben and Jerry's and her firstborn. \"I think my older son was just starting to understand me having a baby in my tummy after accompanying me to my OB appointments and seeing my stomach get bigger,\" she says. \"He joined for the photos, which I think made the whole thing a lot more fun!\"",
        "text_sha256": "5a57604212348ffeb9c973cdeae909e40bdf690bba3faed00491e2dd1eb26285",
        "word_count": 65
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Document an adventure",
        "text_sha256": "2cf013777e368c7d74983c9775b9c3dddad4c9961bf6ffa48679337e928e7431",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "woman and man posing for a photo on a scenic hike",
        "text_sha256": "af428ac7556e1a16a3c3424e27e873e34ebf54d4ffa0bd472a1cbb4931643997",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Travel could look a lot different in the next few months, so why not hit the road now and take some pics on your babymoon ? That's exactly what Sarah Darby , associate director of SEO content strategy at What to Expect, has done during each of her pregnancies. \"It was a perfect time to travel during pregnancy and a great way to reflect and relax while I was still comfortable enough to enjoy the vacation!\" she says.",
        "text_sha256": "b91e68569718c2ac7ceb1ca4f37474fd4d6a76a2eb44509bac3a81527bd10920",
        "word_count": 78
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Use those wooden baby milestone blocks",
        "text_sha256": "9b8e4d9301ed9515e6f82203fbff50b278c60f315351b1a2fa56e35976c217aa",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "pregnant mom holding wooden blocks that say",
        "text_sha256": "23dcba99dcf9aed7176294d1425d21536d3363eff4581c4271b87c7da79ce6f6",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Marifer Fitzpatrick ( @maferfitz ) took out her baby photo shoot props early and posed with them at 20 weeks. \"Pregnancy always feels like a mix of excitement, gratitude, and anticipation, and we wanted to pause and capture this season before life changes again,\" she says.",
        "text_sha256": "fd343e7f4d81d5f876d09f3c19dfb856325bab06171dc76bc46398d6997cd0ce",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In the spirit of simplicity, Fitzpatrick has three non-negotiables: \"natural light, a comfortable outfit, and a calm space make a big difference,\" she says. \"Focus less on perfection and more on documenting the season you're in.\"",
        "text_sha256": "456458e708118a4a4b94178bb73fca741d71a7a4807c1f9309cac4323d5b918e",
        "word_count": 36
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 748,
    "heading_count": 7
  },
  "title": "Inside the Middle-of-Pregnancy Photo Trend Taking Off",
